exports[`salidas de referencia del generador > gift permanece estable en en 1`] = `
"## Role
Act as a teacher specialising in Matemáticas ESO.

## Context
Working with learners in ESO.

## Objective and task
Generate a question bank in GIFT format (Moodle/Aules) about las fracciones.

## Objectives
Operar con fracciones equivalentes.

## Number of questions
10

## Question types
Multiple choice · True/False

## Teacher review
- Deliver a reviewable first draft; do not present it as definitive.
- Use clear, observable instructions appropriate to the level.
- Check that the proposal is feasible with the stated time and resources.
- Flag any data, source or assumption the teacher should verify.
- Do not invent regulations, references or information about learners.

## Output format
Return the result in GIFT.

## Rules for a clean import into Aules and Moodle
Output only the GIFT code: no introduction, no explanations, no code fences and no Markdown.
- Separate questions with a blank line and use a short ASCII name (SR01, SR02...).
- Use only these Aules- and Moodle-compatible types: single-answer multiple choice, true/false and short answer.
- In multiple choice, put each option on its own line with the prefix = (correct) or ~ (incorrect). Never omit that prefix and never leave an option starting with anything else.
- Do not use matching questions with ->, ordering or partial-credit percentages (%): Aules imports them wrongly or fails.
- For true/false, write exactly TRUE or FALSE in braces, with no extra text.
- For short answer, write each accepted answer on its own line preceded by =, with at most three equivalent variants.
- Check that the first character of every answer and the = or ~ prefix have not been lost.
- Do not include HTML, tags, images, audio or external files. Use UTF-8 and escape the characters ~ = # { } : \\ with a backslash when they appear inside a text.
- Do not add // comments or # feedback. Do not include the teacher-review notes inside the GIFT: give them separately, only if asked."
`;

