exports[`salidas de referencia del generador > learning-situation permanece estable en en 1`] = `
"## Role
Act as a teacher specialising in Ciencias Primary 4.º.

## Context
Working with learners in Primary 4.º.

Grupo heterogéneo de 24 estudiantes.

## Specific competences
- Plantear y responder preguntas sobre el entorno.
- Identificar problemas ambientales.

## Objective and task
Design an activity about Los ecosistemas.

## Objectives
Comprender las relaciones de una cadena trófica.

## Methodology
Project-based learning · UDL

## Duration
One session

## Available resources
Tablets · Manipulatives

## Constraints and limits
Una sesión de 45 minutos.

## Quality criteria
Incluye una adaptación de apoyo.

## Assessment criteria
- Formular predicciones y explicaciones.

## Basic knowledge
- Cultura científica · Iniciación a la actividad científica.
- Societats i territoris · Sostenibilidad.

## Universal Design for Learning (UDL)
Design the proposal following Universal Design for Learning (CAST guidelines). For each principle, propose concrete options for the whole group, not just for particular learners, and explain which barrier each one removes.
- Engagement (the why): offer options to spark interest, sustain effort and support self-regulation (choice, relevance, collaboration, frequent feedback).
- Representation (the what): present information in more than one format (text, visual, audio, hands-on), clarify vocabulary and symbols and activate prior knowledge.

## Contextual barriers
Textos largos sin apoyo visual.
Anticipate these barriers in the design without labelling or identifying anyone.

## Teacher review
- Deliver a reviewable first draft; do not present it as definitive.
- Use clear, observable instructions appropriate to the level.
- Check that the proposal is feasible with the stated time and resources.
- Flag any data, source or assumption the teacher should verify.
- Do not invent regulations, references or information about learners.
- Keep the same objective and level of demand for the whole group.
- Check there are at least two ways to access the content and to show what has been learned.

## Output format
Return the result in Markdown."
`;

